      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-12-12T00:43:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confused how this works. If we are sitting here with key scanning disabled, and then scanning suddenly gets enabled, it seems the following will happen:\n- this task will wake\n- we will call keyboard_raw_drive_column(KEYBOARD_COLUMN_ALL)\n- we will check if a key is pressed\n\nBut if no key is pressed we will end up back here in task_wait_event(-1), only we\u0027ve never enabled the keyboard interrupt (keyboard_raw_enable_interrupt(1)). So, how does this wake up then when the user presses a key?\n\nI\u0027m not familiar enough with the key scanning task to know if it\u0027s indirectly enabled somewhere and it seems from comments like there are subtle race conditions enabling that interrupt.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "d3fc4c62dac34db16f672273e7640f94c3ec8552",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5cc3e7f_65e4e063",
        "filename": "common/keyboard_scan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 619,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-12-12T01:10:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure why it was designed that way, but it looks like the interrupt is always left enabled for the duration of the loop.  I left that part of the design in here.\n\nSaid another way:\n* The interrupt is disabled in polling mode\n* The interrupt is enabled in non polling mode regardless of whether the columns are driven or not.\n\nThat\u0027s not insane, actually, because:\n* In polling mode we\u0027re driving 1 column at a time.  I\u0027d presume that the interrupt would be confusing and wasteful here.\n* If we\u0027re not in polling mode and scanning is enabled, we want the interrupt.\n* If we\u0027re not in polling mode and scanning is disabled, the interrupt can\u0027t fire so no reason to disable it.",
      "parentUuid": "c5b81ad7_bce44dd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 24
      },
